    "qbi-deduction-a-practical-guide-for-business-owners/index.html": {
      "title": "QBI Planning for Business Owners: Payroll, Property and 2026 Rules",
      "description": "Compare payroll, spouse wages, property purchases and aggregation using conditional QBI examples. Review 2026 thresholds, rental rules and after-tax costs.",
      "faqs": [
        [
          "Does a $20,000 larger QBI deduction save $20,000 in tax?",
          "No. If the entire additional deduction offsets income taxed at 37%, its federal income-tax value is $7,400. That is before payroll taxes, wage expense, retirement costs, state taxes, and other changes. A deduction increase is not a tax credit or proof of a net saving."
        ],
        [
          "Can a business with no W-2 wages still qualify?",
          "Yes. Below the threshold no wage/property limit applies. Above the phase-in range, a qualifying non-SSTB with zero wages can have capacity from 2.5% of eligible UBIA, subject to the 20% QBI and overall taxable-income limits. Owner-employees still must satisfy reasonable-compensation rules."
        ],
        [
          "Does buying equipment in December give more UBIA than buying in January?",
          "No general monthly proration applies to ordinary calendar-year UBIA. Property must meet the placed-in-service, QBI-use, year-end holding, and depreciable-period requirements. Either month can qualify for the same year; the purchase alone is not enough."
        ],
        [
          "Do I need real estate professional status to deduct rental QBI?",
          "It can qualify as a trade or business, through the rental safe harbor, or under applicable commonly controlled self-rental rules. Real estate professional status is not required. The safe harbor includes books, records, a statement, and 250 rental-service hours annually for newer enterprises or in three of five years for enterprises at least four years old. Related-SSTB restrictions remain separate."
        ],
        [
          "Can I aggregate any businesses I own?",
          "No. The ownership, ownership-period, tax-year, non-SSTB, and operational-link requirements must be met. At least two of three specified operational links are needed, and annual reporting and consistency rules apply. Aggregation does not permit arbitrary reassignment of wages or property basis."
        ]
      ],
      "publication_dates": [
        "2025-04-21T00:00:00-04:00"
      ],
      "baseline_sha256": "8d083f3f3d78229aad200b37eac371c8e5c2dc4fca551d6c967453a048c8c80a",
